Z||000000||Ironhorse||03-22-2000||03:43 PM||||I'm working on buying a 1986 or 87 Fiero se or gt v6 engine either a 4 sp or 5 sp.  My question is that if I buy one that has no sunroof or has sunroof, is there a T-Top conversion that would enable me to take one and with work, cutting, TLC install a T-Top?<P>BTW, I love this Forums, I learned a lot keep up the good work!!!!||||reg||10
Z||000001||87PegasusGT||03-22-2000||06:22 PM||||There are... but you are looking at some serious $$ and hours. My local club has access to 5 more FACTORY kits but they are SPENDY&gt;||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||03-22-2000||06:22 PM||||Ironhourse,<P>This topic has been discussed in great detail in the recent past. If you search the archives, you should find numerous references. But in the meantime, the answer to your question is "yes". But, it'll cost ya. There are, on occasion, T-top kit offered for sale on Ebay. From what I've seen, they are usually pricey. I am one of the lucky few who actually found a complete T-Top car in the local U-Pull-It yard.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> It now resides in the loft area of my garage waiting for me to (some day) install it on my 87 GT. For a little more info, here is a link you may find interesting: <A HREF="http://www.fierottop.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierottop.com/</A>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Good Luck,<BR>RoyL<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Earne||03-22-2000||06:27 PM||||Any new or used T-Top kit will work.  New is better, but a lot more expensive.  Used, trouble with rubber seals, warps in the frame, P seals, scratched glass, etc.<P>Not easy, I bought a new kit from and am having Bob Steiger of Twin Lakes Fiero install mine.  I'm good at what I do, but it doesn't include cutting my Fiero nearly in half.  My 86.5 GT has a sunroof and it is completely removed during the installation.  Part of the kit includes an H-frame that is riveted and sealed in place.  This gives the support to the space frame that cutting out the side top rails would normally provide.  The only part of the H-frame you see is the divider between the two glass tops.  <P>This is not a job that should be tackled by the inexperienced or faint of heart.  You need jigs for proper spacing and a method for prying the front and rear remaining roof sections apart to fit the new top frame in place.  I just got off the phone with Bob and he says that with the other work he has going, to count on 2-3 weeks for the installation.  Hope this helps.  By the way, a used kit can cost as little as the price of removing the parts from a junk or wreck.  New can cost up to $3,000.  There are VERY few new kits left.  Installation by a pro will be $1000 plus.  That's a lot of money but a few of the guys here know my car and I'm thinkin' its worth it.<P>Just imagine guys, all that gleaming silver and chrome and a brand new set of tops?  Any comments.  The car will be a Bob's later this week, I'll post pics when I pick it up.<p>[This message has been edited by Earne (edited 03-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||03-22-2000||06:29 PM||||It is definitely doable, but as everyone else has already said....it'll be expensive.  You will be money ahead if you just buy a Fiero with the T-Tops already installed.  If you scour the national classifieds (online or otherwise) you will come across some really good deals.  Some basic coupes with T-Tops can be had for just a few hundred dollars and even some V-6 models in the $1000 range.  Even if you have to convert it to a V-6 and/or convert the body to the style you prefer you will still come out cheaper than installing a kit on a Fiero.  <P>I did this several years ago to a Formula.  I paid $2100 for the Formula and $2500 for T-Tops (installed)!  Ouch.....it still hurts to think about it and that was 4 years ago!     ||||reg||14
Z||000005||Ironhorse||03-22-2000||09:17 PM||||Hmm.. Thanks for the quick replies.  The way I see it I can do one of three things. 1) Buy Fiero with T top from factory. 2) Start playin lottery to buy one and have it put in. Or 3)Don't bother, why mess with perfection  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
